{"kind":"assert","text":"CTL-1 precode plan only, checked at main bc79b6aabb24d98e5e379fd5006de6ee9464682f. No source edit, promise, execution, or delivery claim.\n\nExactly three source files:\n1. scripts/control.mjs: readVitest currently joins failureMessages then truncates to 300 characters (117–118,164–167), and isAssertion accepts only a headline starting AssertionError. Keep display truncation separate from assertion classification. On Vitest failures, recognize the complete anchored constructor message before truncation: Error: promise rejected \"\u003cinspect payload\u003e\" instead of resolving, or Error: promise resolved \"\u003cinspect payload\u003e\" instead of rejecting. Require the exact direction and terminal phrase, not substring matches or a general Error prefix. Preserve the existing AssertionError path, Node TAP authority, timeout precedence, baseline/load/count checks, --expect selection, restoration, and raw output.\n\nThe pinned @vitest/expect is 4.1.12. Its resolves constructor is dist/index.js:1732, rejects constructor:1767; catch handlers at1735–1738 and1776–1778 replace AssertionError.stack with an earlier Error stack. File SHA256 b177ca97952f1d65d3d2691edbc31ab1af56ac36b3cf08d7f56ad0ca69f07a45. The pinned JSON reporter at vitest/dist/chunks/index.UpGiHP7g.js:3559–3583 emits failureMessages from e.stack || e.message (3573), but no per-error name. JsonAssertionResult at reporters.d.DtoKVV2s.d.ts:2297–2306 confirms that shape. fullName/title and the containing file name are test names, not error names. Therefore this pin requires the approved exact fallback. If an actual supported report supplies an error name, use that name before fallback; do not invent a failureDetails/errors field or change reporters merely to obtain it. An exact counterfeit constructor message is indistinguishable once this JSON reporter discards the error name; the fallback cannot promise constructor identity.\n\n2. scripts/control.test.mjs: reuse the existing real pinn